// Forbid bare `/api/...` URL literals appearing as a JSX attribute value
// (`href="/api/foo"`, `action="/api/foo"`, etc.) in site/ code. Sibling
// rule to `no-direct-api-fetch-in-site.grit` — same root cause, different
// surface (direct-navigation targets rather than `fetch()` calls).
//
// Previews and prod live on different origins from the API: the front
// sits on a static-site CloudFront distribution that serves only the
// bundle; the API has its own custom domain
// (`*-api.preview.borso.fr` / `api.borso.fr`). A bare `/api/...` literal
// in a JSX `href` therefore opens the static-site CDN, which has no
// `/api/*` behaviour and falls through to the SPA 404 page.
//
// First observed in PR #27, where the new "Stats par boucle (CSV)"
// button and the pre-existing "Classement (CSV)" button both 404'd on
// preview while the underlying endpoint returned 200. Symptoms + causal
// chain in docs/dantotsus/api-anchor-must-use-api-url-on-preview.md.
//
// Implementation notes
// --------------------
// JSX attribute strings parse to a `JsxString` AST node, NOT to a normal
// `JsLiteralExpression`. The template `"$_"` only matches the JS string
// shape, so the `\`"/api/$_"\`` pattern used by the sibling fetch plugin
// silently misses every JSX attribute. The right shape is to match
// `JsxString()` directly, then filter the token's literal text with a
// regex.
//
// The literal text of a `JsxString` includes the surrounding quotes —
// e.g. for `<a href="/api/foo">`, `$s` literally equals `"/api/foo"`.
// The regex therefore looks for the `/api/` substring INSIDE the quote
// delimiters: `.*\"/api/.*` matches `"/api/foo"` and `'/api/foo'` after
// substring search.
//
// `engine biome(1.0)` + `language js(jsx)` are required — without them
// the JSX AST nodes are invisible to the pattern engine. Cf. biome's
// own test fixtures crates/biome_grit_patterns/tests/specs/tsx/.
//
// Allowed:
//   <a href={apiUrl('/api/foo')}>…</a>   // string is JS, not JSX
//   <a href="https://…">…</a>            // explicit absolute URL
//   <a href={someVariableUrl}>…</a>      // not a literal — out of scope
//
// Forbidden:
//   <a href="/api/…">…</a>
//   <a href='/api/…'>…</a>

engine biome(1.0)
language js(jsx)

JsxString() as $s where {
  $s <: r".*[\"']/api/.*",
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $s,
    message = "Bare `/api/...` in a JSX attribute bypasses VITE_API_BASE and 404s on preview (cross-origin API hostname). Wrap with `apiUrl('/api/...')` from `api/client.ts` — eg `href={apiUrl('/api/foo')}`. See docs/dantotsus/api-anchor-must-use-api-url-on-preview.md.",
    severity = "error"
  )
}
